	// client's inference: it is the rulebook's own predicate, the same question
	// a monster's mind asks when it decides whether it can shoot from where it
	// stands. A palette offering a "ranged / melee / both" filter reads this
	// bool rather than looking for "ranged" inside `category`. The day the
	// rulebook spells a ranged category some other way, this stays true and that
	// substring hunt breaks.
	//
	// The filter is a palette convenience that WRITES A WEAPON LIST and is never
